Subject: round: Site Search chips, Collapse Pinned Tabs, New Documents

Three more items on the operator's word, built together.

Site Search (S-109, commandbar K27): typing a search engine's keyword,
name or domain offers "Search <name>", Tab makes a chip and only that
engine's rows show; the @bookmarks and @history scopes need their whole
keyword, so short prefixes keep Tab for the actions and "@" stays the
Space filter. The list is Chromium's own search engine settings; no AI
scopes (ADR 0020).

Collapse Pinned Tabs (S-114, pins H17): from the Space menu or the bar,
per Space, kept in the registry across a restart; the pins hide by the
one row rule and the selected pin keeps its row.

New Documents (S-116, commandbar K28): bar rows for eleven services'
blank documents through their .new addresses.

Why: the operator asked for the next three; each has its behaviour id
and tests.
Removable when: never; these are Stedding's own behaviours.
